  "context": "# Round\nkasegi-shokunin round 31, dispatched by the L1 (agent KasegiR31) via the inline spawn handoff (hyaku run 7). Lane repo /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kasegi-shokunin is your ONLY write scope. Lane base b374febbb33ccadade78a787279707fd5d2e6e1d; claims-freeze commit 738a77999a00efbca129cfccb28a481037f6241f. The fleet root /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin is read-only to you.\n\nFrozen claims (do not edit; corrections land as separate appended files): /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kasegi-shokunin/.ufo/waves/round-31/claims.json\n- C1 depth:verifiability (score 4, held): a new one-limb mutation ledger `corpus/instruments/limb-ledger.json` + counter `corpus/instruments/limb-mutation-check.py` must print `limbs=13 killed=13 survivors=0` and `controls=3 rejected=3`, exit 0, with 13 `LIMB ` lines, each live-result != mutant-result.\n- C2 coverage (score 7, held): Frontier F15 (Microsoft MSVR as an intake route for other vendors' bugs) admitted 14 -> 15, new row S048 (registry 47 -> 48), one knowledge entry citing S048, harness entries=18 pass=18, census exit 0, source-recheck S048 exit 0 on corpus/source-snapshots/round-31/manifest.json.\n- Non-claim frontier items: assimilation (theme = vendor third-party-finding coordination; staged S080 -> lane S048 by DOCUMENT, collision scratch in /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kasegi-shokunin/.ufo/waves/round-31/assimilation/), considerthese proposal 2 (score-gap, read-only), mistake M31-1 (stale-premise: SCORECARD round-30 'recheck-audit open item exit=1' paragraph + missing round-30 LOG entry).\n\nRead as your item requires (absolute paths): /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kasegi-shokunin/.ufo/waves/round-31/claims.json; /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kasegi-shokunin/corpus/QUALITY.md (entry bar Q1-Q10, record R1-R15); /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kasegi-shokunin/corpus/SOURCES.md; /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kasegi-shokunin/corpus/README.md; /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kasegi-shokunin/corpus/instruments/README.md and the instruments; /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kasegi-shokunin/corpus/lessons/round-30.md and round-30-verifier-spotcheck.md; /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kasegi-shokunin/considerthese/2026-10-25.md (proposals only); read-only campaign package /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokuknow/merge/kasegi/ (never write there, never run its tools).\n\n## INTERFACE CONTRACT for C1 (frozen by the L1; every C1 seat codes to this)\nLedger file `/home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kasegi-shokunin/corpus/instruments/limb-ledger.json`:\n{\"version\":1,\"limbs\":[LIMB...],\"controls\":[CONTROL...]}\nLIMB = {\"id\":\"RA-parse\",\"instrument\":\"corpus/instruments/recheck-audit.py\",\"find\":\"<exact text occurring EXACTLY ONCE in the instrument>\",\"replace\":\"<mutant text>\",\"kill\":\"<shell command, cwd = scratch lane copy; placeholder {inst} = the instrument path inside the scratch copy (mutated or not); other placeholder {root} = scratch lane root>\",\"live_exit\":0,\"signal\":\"<python regex that MUST match the unmutated run's stdout+stderr>\",\"note\":\"<what the limb is>\"}\nCONTROL = {\"id\":\"CTL-noop|CTL-nocompile|CTL-equivalent\",\"instrument\":\"...\",\"find\":\"...\",\"replace\":\"...\",\"kill\":\"...\",\"live_exit\":0,\"signal\":\"...\",\"expect\":\"invalid:noop|invalid:nocompile|survivor\"}\nCounter `python3 corpus/instruments/limb-mutation-check.py --ledger <path> [--root <lane>]` semantics: copy `<root>/corpus` (plus any file a kill command needs) into a fresh tempfile.mkdtemp scratch lane; for each row run the kill command on the UNMUTATED scratch (must exit live_exit and match signal, else verdict `invalid:live-baseline`), then apply the find/replace to the scratch copy of the instrument and run the kill command again. Verdicts per row, printed one per line exactly as `LIMB <id> live=<exit>/<sig:y|n> mutant=<exit>/<sig:y|n> verdict=killed|survivor|invalid:<reason>`: `invalid:find-count` when find does not occur exactly once; `invalid:noop` when the mutated bytes equal the original; `invalid:nocompile` when `py_compile` of the mutated file fails; `killed` when the mutant's (exit != live_exit) or (signal does not match); else `survivor`. Controls print `CONTROL <id> verdict=<v> expected=<e> ok=y|n`. Summary lines, exactly: `limbs=<n> killed=<k> survivors=<s>` and `controls=<n> rejected=<r>` (rejected counts controls whose verdict equals expect). Exit 0 iff n==k, s==0, every limb valid, and rejected==controls. The counter NEVER writes into the lane tree (scratch only; delete scratch at exit) and runs no git write. Python stdlib only.\nThe 13 limbs (ids fixed): RA-parse, RA-cwd, RA-paths (recheck-audit frozen limbs a,b,c); RA-cdroot, RA-instrument, RA-own (strict limbs d,e,f); RA-completeness, RA-expect-missing, RA-expect-unexpected; SR-stem-mismatch, SR-occurrence-not-unique (source-recheck.py); FR-missing-entry, FR-duplicate-entry (frontier-recheck-count.py). A limb with no failing kill signal today is a SURVIVOR: the owning executor strengthens the instrument's own selftest/fixtures (a new case that fails only on that limb) so the mutant is killed - that strengthening IS the work. If a limb is provably equivalent (no observable behavior), report it as such with proof; never relabel a survivor as killed.\n\n## WAVE 2 SCOPE (falsify wave; wave 1 has landed and is quiescent: read its receipts under /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kasegi-shokunin/.ufo/waves/round-31/wave1/)\nSeats are READ-ONLY on the lane except these single-writer paths: /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kasegi-shokunin/corpus/instruments/limb-mutation-check.py and limb-ledger.json: ExecCounterFix (fixes only) | /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kasegi-shokunin/corpus/QUALITY.md: ScribeQualityFix (fixes only) | /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kasegi-shokunin/corpus/lessons/round-31.md: ScribeLesson | /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kasegi-shokunin/SCORECARD.md: ScribeScorecard (append-only) | /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kasegi-shokunin/SHONEN.md: ScribeShonen | every /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kasegi-shokunin/.ufo/waves/round-31/wave2/<YourName>.md receipt: its own seat. All attack work happens in mktemp scratch copies; never edit instruments, entries, registry, README, SKILL.md or PROVINCE.md (report defects; the L1 routes fixes).\n\nBounds (all seats):\n1. Writes go ONLY under /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kasegi-shokunin - never the fleet root, sibling lanes, lane jj state or lane Git index, /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokuknow (read-only; never run campaign tools there), templates/, scripts/, .ufo/state/, .ufo/watchdog.log, MANIFEST.json, /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/.scratch/.\n2. Every `Report:` trailer path is relative to /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kasegi-shokunin - write it at /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kasegi-shokunin/<that path> (= /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kasegi-shokunin/.ufo/waves/round-31/wave2/<YourName>.md). Receipts hold commands + their output, never prose-only claims.\n3. Never message agent://all; coordinate only with the peers named in your item via write agent://<id> (id = the seat name).\n4. NEVER run git/jj mutations in the lane (no add/commit/stash/checkout/reset/pull/push, no jj commit/new/describe/squash/rebase/abandon/bookmark/undo). The L1 commits through the lane helper. Read-only git (log, show, diff, status, ls-files, rev-parse) is fine. Git fixtures: D=$(mktemp -d) && git -C \"$D\" init -q; verify `git -C \"$D\" rev-parse --show-toplevel` equals $D before the first commit; every later git call names -C \"$D\"; never a throwaway identity anywhere else.\n5. Tooling authorization (operator 2026-10-19): you may install/upgrade tools that help the task - read /home/vgpnk/.omp/agent/RULES.md first (official channels; record tool/version/channel/reason in your receipt). pacman is PAUSED host-wide (orchestrator ruling 2026-10-20): never run any pacman transaction; use uv tool/npx/an official binary in ~/.local/bin. Never -Sy/-Syu/-U/-R, no downgrade, no host-service restart.\n6. A counter run before its subject lands is PRE-STATE: label it so, name the re-run, never compare a PRE-STATE number to an after column. In-flight outputs while another seat edits are non-comparative (M30-3): re-run on quiescent bytes before you cite.\n7. Leaf role: no delegation, no background jobs, no own swarm; an executor may spawn at most one read-only labrat probe.\n8. Documentation-only domain: never contact any live bounty target; fetches are limited to the public documentation URLs your item names (instrument UA: `kasegi-shokunin/1.0 (documentation capture; +https://shokunin.invalid/kasegi)`). No credential material, session URLs or vault references in any file.\n9. Waiting: when your item says wait for a peer receipt, poll with `until [ -s <file> ]; do sleep 20; done` (cap 30 minutes); if the file never appears, record `BLOCKED: <file>` in your receipt and finish what you can. Do not busy-loop.\n10. Record the answering model you actually ran on when your item depends on it (the config route table decides; never pass a model).\n11. Quote discipline (CORPUS.md rule 1, QUALITY Q3): a quote is <=25 words with its exact location; never retype a number from memory.",
