      "task": "/skill:godspeed\n\nFalsify ledger limb `RA-parse` (recheck-audit frozen limb (a) parse) of the C1 ledger on the LANDED bytes. Wave-1 landed the counter /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kasegi-shokunin/corpus/instruments/limb-mutation-check.py and ledger /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kasegi-shokunin/corpus/instruments/limb-ledger.json (read-only for you; all work in a mktemp scratch copy of /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kasegi-shokunin/corpus). (1) Re-derive by hand: read the ledger row id `RA-parse`, copy /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kasegi-shokunin/corpus to a scratch dir, run the row's kill command on the UNMUTATED copy (record exit + whether `signal` matches), apply the row's find/replace yourself with python (assert find occurs exactly once; `python3 -m py_compile` the result), run the kill command again, and compare with the counter's `LIMB RA-parse ...` line from `python3 corpus/instruments/limb-mutation-check.py --ledger corpus/instruments/limb-ledger.json` (run it in the lane; it is scratch-only). Any difference between your hand result and the counter's line is a defect. (2) Discrimination: design a SECOND, different one-limb mutant of the same limb (different code site or inversion) and run the kill command - say whether it is killed; if the instrument's own cases kill only one specific mutant shape, say so. (3) Isolation: show the limb's mutant is killed by a case that is specific to this limb (list which output lines differ), not by an unrelated crash: the mutant run must still print the instrument's normal banner/other cases. Write /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kasegi-shokunin/.ufo/waves/round-31/wave2/ExecLimbRAparse.md with commands, outputs and a verdict `holds|weak|defect`.\n\nLane bounds: leaf member — no subagent dispatch except your single labrat.\nJudged on: depth:verifiability, coverage\nMilestone: round-31\n\nReport: write your scoped findings to .ufo/waves/round-31/wave2/ExecLimbRAparse.md"
    },
    {
